From 62ebdc13ec379d605fb2349051161a35ad10946a Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: Dimitri Geelen <dimitri@geelenandcompany.com>
Date: Sun, 4 Oct 2026 14:18:10 +0200
Subject: [PATCH 10/10] [PROPOSAL, not drop-in] inception decide: a GO requires
 a falsifiable ## Hypothesis (from 832 T-866/T-1026)
MIME-Version: 1.0
Content-Type: text/plain; charset=UTF-8
Content-Transfer-Encoding: 8bit

A GO is the moment a project takes on a claim. 832 requires that claim in three-part form, with a
success clause naming something someone could go and look at; NO-GO and DEFER take on no claim
and are not gated. audit_inception_hypothesis (lib/task-audit.sh) checks the form (research-kind
inceptions are exempt, and the word "research" in the body does not exempt). The gate in
do_inception_decide sits after the Recommendation gate and fails CLOSED if the audit lib did not
load: a gate whose absence looks like a pass is the defect.
Probe: tests/unit/test_t1021_hypothesis_gate.sh. Before: refuses (the function does not exist).
After: 10/10.

WHY THIS IS A PROPOSAL: it changes your governance, and it breaks 17 of your tests in 8 suites,
because their fixtures record a GO with no ## Hypothesis (or, in t3641, expect the readiness
lib's wording for a missing lib before ours fires):
  inception_decide_atomicity.bats 1,2 · inception_decide_auto_create_decision_section.bats 1,2 ·
  inception_decide_emit_review_post_move.bats 1 · inception_decide_propagate_exit.bats 1,2,3 ·
  inception_decide_recommendation_gate.bats 8 · t2862_greenfield_first_inception_e2e.bats 1,3,4,5 ·
  t3279_decision_readiness_parity.bats 6,8 · t3641_readiness_fail_closed.bats 7,8
If you adopt the rule, those fixtures need a hypothesis; if you do not, drop this commit. The
other commits in this series do not depend on it. The other 34 suites touching inception decide
or task-audit are unchanged; audit_blocks_review_and_decide.bats #3 fails on both sides.
